  "prediction": "**Multiple Arrests Made in Robeson County Arson Investigation**\n\nIn a shocking turn of events, 10 volunteer firefighters from the Fairmont and Orrum Fire Departments in Robeson County, North Carolina, have been arrested and charged with intentionally setting fires to abandoned homes and woods over a two-year period. The investigation, led by the Robeson County Sheriff's Office, State Bureau of Investigation, Alcohol, Tobacco and Firearms, and the NC Forestry Service, resulted in approximately 90 arson-related charges, with more expected.\n\nThe arrested individuals, all of whom are volunteer firefighters, include:\n\n1. Melquan Williams, 21, of Fairmont, charged with one count of felony arson and one count of felony conspiracy, with a bond set at $200,000.\n2. Austin Seth Hunt, 23, of Rowland, charged with six counts of felony arson and five counts of felony conspiracy, with a bond set at $200,000.\n3. Ashley Marie Oxendine, 18, of Orrum, charged with two counts of felony arson and two counts of felony conspiracy, with a bond set at $100,000.\n4. John Austin Huggins, 17, of Fairmont, charged with two counts of felony arson and two counts of felony conspiracy, with a bond set at $100,000.\n5. Jordan Scott, 19, of Fairmont, charged with four counts of felony arson and four counts of felony conspiracy, with a bond set at $100,000.\n6. Kenny Caulder Jr., 19, of Fairmont, charged with five counts of felony arson and four counts of felony conspiracy, with a bond set at $100,000.\n7. Willie Fuentes Strickland, 42, of Fairmont, charged with two counts of felony arson and one count of felony conspiracy, with a bond set at $100,000.\n8. Jordan Emmanuel Hunt, 18, of Fairmont, charged with four counts of felony arson and four counts of felony conspiracy, with a bond set at $100,000.\n9. Shellia Huggins, 19, of Fairmont, charged with two counts of felony arson and two counts of felony conspiracy, with a bond set at $100,000.\n10. William Kendall Strickland, 18, of Fairmont, charged with one count of misdemeanor larceny and one count of felony conspiracy, with a bond set at $100,000.\n\nThe investigation was sparked by a tip and has been ongoing",
